WEBVTT

english-main-idea-supporting-details-narration-caption-1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.415
Show me: name the topic, then add what the author wants us to understand about it. ‘City trees’ is only the topic; the main idea explains their benefits.

english-main-idea-supporting-details-narration-caption-2
00:00:08.415 --> 00:00:17.325
Talk me through it: after naming the topic, test each possible main idea against the important details. Keep the idea that works as an umbrella over most of them.

english-main-idea-supporting-details-narration-caption-3
00:00:17.325 --> 00:00:29.325
Let’s do one together. Bees carry pollen between flowers. This helps many plants produce fruits and seeds. Farms and wild habitats both depend on that work. Which main idea works as an umbrella over all three sentences?

english-main-idea-supporting-details-narration-caption-4
00:00:29.325 --> 00:00:37.080
Different example: science observations, fresh food, and teamwork all fit under one idea—that a school garden helps a school in several ways.
